# THE LEAK SCAN for the public tree (scripts/ops/publish-public-repo.sh --check). Every copied TEXT file is matched line by line
# against every pattern below; ONE hit fails the publish. The scan is the second gate behind the allowlist: the allowlist decides
# which files leave, this file catches a private word, host or key path that slipped into one of them.
#
# Format: one JavaScript regex literal per line, `/pattern/flags`, optionally followed by `allow: <path> <path>` naming published
# paths where that pattern is expected and permitted (each exemption must be justified in a comment above it). This file itself
# and the allowlist are never scanned (they contain the words by construction).

# the private trading platform: its directories, its arming flags, its arm names
/\bexperimental\b/i
/\barming\b/i
/\bXRH_/
/\bXSOL/
# Robinhood as a TRADING ARM (the chain name alone is allowed: the refuse list covers every chain the bots trade, which is the point)
/robinhood[\s_-]*(arm|book|runner|bot|trading|live|paper|signer|keygen)\b/i
/\brh-(live|signer|keygen|runner|paper)\b/i allow: test/burntickerOps.test.ts
/\bRH_[A-Z0-9_]+/
/\b(xrh|xsol|xbnb|xarc|xsolrr|xsolscalp)\b/i

# local env FILES (.env, .env.local …; `process.env.X` is code, not a file) and the private RPC variable (the public code reads
# BURNKEEPER_RPC_URL / BURNTICKER_RPC_URL only). .gitignore must ignore env files in the public repo too — the one place the name is wanted
/(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])\.env(\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)?\b/ allow: .gitignore config/public-repo/overlay/.gitignore test/burntickerOps.test.ts docs/burnticker/deploy.md docs/burnticker/runbook.md docs/burnticker/REHEARSAL-RUNSHEET.md deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-keeper.service deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-web.service scripts/load-env.sh scripts/service/run-burnkeeper.sh scripts/service/run-burnticker-keeper.sh scripts/service/run-burnticker-web.sh scripts/ops/install-burnticker-units.sh docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-10-pair-curve-blind-1.md docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-10-pair-curve-recheck.md
# (the host's units and entrypoints READ that host's env file by name — load-env.sh is the reader; none of them contains a value)
# (operator docs name the host's env FILE so the owner knows where variables go; they never contain a value — the trading repo's env files are never published)
# (the ops test ASSERTS that the keeper never reads an env file and that the ship script excludes them — the names appear only inside those assertions)
# (blind review 1 of pair_curve states, as a scope note, that no env FILE was touched — a sentence about the method, no value)
/SOLANA_RPC_URL/

# key material and private key paths
/-----BEGIN /
/\bid_ed25519\b/
/\.pem\b/
/\/Users\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\//
/\/home\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\//
/\/root\//
# a raw 64-byte secret key as JSON, or as base58 (a transaction signature has the same length: a fixture's obviously padded
# placeholder — twenty identical characters in a row — is not a key; a real signature in a fixture must be exempted by path)
/\[\s*(\d{1,3}\s*,\s*){63}\d{1,3}\s*\]/
# (the devnet rehearsal records, 2026-10-10 — the morning run and the pair_curve run: these tokens are devnet TRANSACTION SIGNATURES. scripts/ops/verify-evidence-signatures.mjs
#  checks that every 86–88-char base58 token in these files decodes to 64 bytes and is a confirmed devnet transaction, and that the
#  evidence directory holds no 64-number array and no secret/keypair field — re-run it whenever these files change)
/\b(?![1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]*([1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z])\1{19})[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{86,88}\b/ allow: docs/burnkeeper/devnet-run-log-2026-10-10.md docs/burnkeeper/devnet-run.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/burns.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/claim.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-1.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-2.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-3.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-sell-1.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/init-token.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/keeper-loop.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/launch.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/platform.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/register.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/status.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/twap-trades.log docs/burnkeeper/devnet-paircurve-run-log-2026-10-10.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-crank-1a.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-crank-1b.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1a.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1b.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-crank-graduate.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-init.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-1-buy-A.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-2-buy-B.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-4-buy-B.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-5-buy-A.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-6-sell-A.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-trade-7-buy-A.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair2